  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 146 AM MDT Fri May 8 2026\n\nMain impact today will again be breezy conditions this afternoon\nwith a Lake Wind Advisory in effect for the American Falls\nReservoir. 15 to 25 mph winds with gusts up to 35 mph expected\nagain this afternoon in the Snake River Plain along with higher\nmountain peaks. It will remain very warm with highs in the 60s\nmountains and 70s valleys. The entirety of the forecast the main\nfeature will be extreme warmth. Saturday will be the coolest day\nof the next week with highs still well into the 60s mountains\nand 70s valleys. By Sunday most low elevations will reach the\n80s and Tuesday looks to be the hottest day with many low\nelevations possibly reaching 90. Will cool down slightly\nWednesday through next Friday but not much with many highs still\nreaching into the 80s so well above normal conditions for the \nnext 8 days. After today will see the breeziest conditions next\nMonday. Overall minimal impacts and very dry conditions through\nthe next week.",
